Package: mitcad
Version: 0.70.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: MitCad Project <maintainer@mitcad.org>
Description: Open source parametric desktop CAD application
 MitCad is a parametric 3D CAD application that runs on Windows, Linux and macOS.
 It features sketch-driven constraints and dimensions, a feature timeline,
 and support for many file formats including STEP, IGES, BRep, STL, OBJ, DXF,
 3MF, FreeCAD (.f3d/.FCStd), SolidCraft (.sc), IPT, IFC, and RVT.
 .
 MitCad includes a tabbed toolbar, command panels with live preview, a browser,
  timeline, and command search functionality. It supports 3D printing through
 direct slicer integration and renders using a path-traced view with optional
 Cycles CUDA/Metal GPU acceleration.
 .
 This package provides the main MitCad application executable and required
 runtime libraries. It does NOT bundle development dependencies.
 .
 The application is GUI-based and requires a desktop environment with Qt6 support.
 It integrates with the system through a .desktop launcher, icons, and MIME type
 associations for design files.
 .
 WWW: https://mitcad.org/
